    {
      "id": "Sticky Note",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -620,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 500,
        "height": 900,
        "content": "## Turn form submissions into branded PDF reports\n\nAn n8n Form takes a field report and PDFMint hands back a finished, branded PDF —\nno headless browser to run and no template editor to log into.\n\n**What it does**\nThe form collects a title, an author, an optional site and the findings. The\nworkflow refuses an incomplete submission before it spends anything, checks the\nPDFMint account still has documents left this month, assembles the Markdown\n(title block, a word-count and reading-time line, findings, an optional\nrecommendation and your footer), renders it, and shows the result. If PDFMint\ncannot be reached, the person who filled the form is told why instead of\nstaring at a blank page.\n\n**Set up**\n1. Add a PDFMint credential — the free plan is 10 documents a month and needs no card.\n2. Open **Set report branding** and put in your own company, accent colour and footer.\n3. Activate, then open the production form URL.\n\n**Requirements**\n- A PDFMint API key from pdf.mintapis.com.\n- This template uses a community node, so it runs on **self-hosted n8n only**.\n\n**Disclosure**\nI build and run PDFMint. This is a self-submission, not a third-party recommendation."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note1",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -60,
        -180
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## 1. Collect and check\nThe form gathers the report. **Set report branding** is the one node you edit. An incomplete submission is refused here, before any credit is spent."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note2",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        840,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 620,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## 2. Is there quota left?\nPDFMint's `usage` operation costs nothing and reports `credits_remaining` for the plan. Asking first turns a silent failure into a sentence the submitter can act on."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note3",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1460,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## 3. Build and render\nThe Code node assembles the Markdown — title block, word count and reading time, findings, optional recommendation, footer. PDFMint turns it into a PDF with margins and page numbers."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "Sticky Note4",
